# Act 1, chapter 1 "Red Ribbon Science": the drone's field test on the Red Ribbon proving ground (areas 1:90-94, 1:84,
# 1:85; generated by log4/gen_ch1.py). Flags: 352 range briefing, 353-355 target sites A-C, 356 heavy tank destroyed,
# 357 arena arrival, 358 all sites announced, 372-373 supply crates, 309 chapter over (report).
# The drone terminal in the main lab (1:61): sends the drone to the range until the tank is destroyed.
list lab_terminal
if_flag 356 term_done
unless_flag 352 term_first
narrate The drone terminal links back to the proving ground. Remote control: on.
goto term_send
label term_first
narrate The drone terminal hums to life. Targeting array: three degrees off true.
say young_gero.0 The drift only shows under fire. Bench tests will never find it.
say young_gero.1 Very well. Then the drone goes out to the proving ground, and the infantry can shoot at it for a change.
label term_send
# skills: the drone keeps Energy Blast (7) and Energy Punch (8) - not Goten's Super Saiyan (20) or Kamekameha (16);
# Gero keeps Energy Blast only - not Goku's Kamehameha (15) or Instant Transmission (14). Removing a missing skill is harmless; joining (151) resets a new member's list, so remove after it.
do call 151 2; call 149 2; call 152 0
do call 165 2 20; call 165 2 16; call 165 0 15; call 165 0 14
do call 120 30
do call 120 1; call 119 1 90 1 166 124; call 121 40
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label term_done
narrate Targeting array: aligned. Calibration complete.
# ---------- the range
list ch1_brief
set_flag 352
narrate Red Ribbon Proving Ground, twenty miles north of headquarters.
narrate Range Sergeant: So that's the doctor's flying toaster. Orders from Commander Red, Doctor: the infantry trains against it today. Live rounds.
narrate Dr. Gero (radio): Good. Your men will be the drone's targets as much as it is theirs, Sergeant.
narrate Range Sergeant: Three target sites out there, each with a grounded sensor drone. Collect data from all three and we'll open the live-fire arena.
journal Record sensor data at three {c07}target sites{c02} on the range
do call 47; call 51 0
list range_sergeant
if_flag 358 sarge_arena
narrate Range Sergeant: Target sites: the Target Field at the top of the canyon road, the Fuel Depot down the south trail, and the Bone Flats past the Pit to the east.
narrate Range Sergeant: The save pad's behind me if you want to file your progress, Doctor.
stop
label sarge_arena
narrate Range Sergeant: The arena's open, west end of the Bone Flats. Word is the Commander put twenty zeni on the tank.
list site_a
if_flag 353 site_seen
set_flag 353
narrate A grounded sensor drone sits in the scorched crater, logging every shot fired on the field. Its data uploads to the drone.
narrate Dr. Gero (radio): Two point eight degrees of drift under fire. Exactly what I expected.
run ch1_sites
stop
label site_seen
narrate The sensor drone's data has already been collected.
list site_b
if_flag 354 site_seen_b
set_flag 354
narrate A grounded sensor drone is parked by the fuel tanks. Its data uploads to the drone.
narrate Dr. Gero (radio): Heat shimmer bends the beam. Another degree. Good.
run ch1_sites
stop
label site_seen_b
narrate The sensor drone's data has already been collected.
list site_c
if_flag 355 site_seen_c
set_flag 355
narrate A grounded sensor drone sits half buried in the crater. Its data uploads to the drone.
narrate Dr. Gero (radio): Recoil from the cannon throws the barrel off by the rest. Three degrees. Found it.
run ch1_sites
stop
label site_seen_c
narrate The sensor drone's data has already been collected.
list ch1_sites
unless_flag 353 sites_wait
unless_flag 354 sites_wait
unless_flag 355 sites_wait
if_flag 358 sites_wait
set_flag 358
narrate Range control (radio): All three sites reporting, Doctor. The live-fire arena is open, west end of the Bone Flats.
journal Pass the final test in the {c07}live-fire arena{c02}
stop
label sites_wait
narrate Range control (radio): Reading received.
list arena_locked
narrate A steel range gate, locked. A sign: LIVE-FIRE ARENA. ALL TARGET SITES MUST REPORT BEFORE ENTRY.
list crate_depot
if_flag 372 crate_empty
set_flag 372
narrate A supply crate somebody forgot to lock. Inside: two cans of soda and a bottle of tea.
do call 129 2 2; call 129 1 1
stop
label crate_empty
narrate The crate is empty.
list crate_pit
if_flag 373 drum_empty
set_flag 373
narrate A dented supply drum. Inside: a carton of milk, and another.
do call 129 0 2
stop
label drum_empty
narrate The drum is empty.
list ch1_arena
set_flag 357
narrate Range control (radio): Final test, Doctor. The army's new heavy tank. Commander Red has money on the tank.
narrate Dr. Gero (radio): Then Commander Red is about to lose his money.
journal Destroy the {c07}heavy tank{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
# ---------- back in the lab (the tank's death script loads 1:61; this walk-in trigger runs while 356 is set and 309 clear)
list ch1_report
set_flag 309
do call 151 0; call 149 0; call 152 2
narrate Dr. Gero's laboratory. On the monitor, the heavy tank is still burning.
narrate Lab technician: Doctor... Commander Red is on the line. He is not pleased. That was his favourite tank.
say young_gero.0 Then he should have built a better one. Three degrees, corrected. The drones are ready.
say young_gero.3 Gevo will have them by dawn.
journal Chapter 1 complete
run ch2_start
# ---------- army file 1 (log4/gen_more.py: the Fuel Depot 1:85; flag 510)
list file_range
if_flag 510 frange_read
set_flag 510
narrate Army file: a requisition order taped to the fuel tank, signed Commander Red himself.
narrate "Effective today, every Dragon Ball expedition takes priority over the android program. Dr. Gero's budget is halved."
say young_gero.3 Halved. For a wish. Whatever that fool wants from the dragon, it isn't victory.
do call 129 29 1
run files_check
stop
label frange_read
narrate Red's order. Gero has it memorised.
